{
 "total": 33.17,
 "planned": false,
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "This fish has eyes almost as big as its head.",
   "visual": "hook",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.383
  },
  {
   "text": "It's called the owlfish.",
   "visual": "name",
   "start": 2.383,
   "end": 3.766
  },
  {
   "text": "It's a deep-sea fish about the size of your hand.",
   "visual": "size",
   "start": 3.766,
   "end": 6.256
  },
  {
   "text": "It lives in the North Pacific, far below the surface.",
   "visual": "depth",
   "start": 6.256,
   "end": 9.202
  },
  {
   "text": "Down there, almost no sunlight reaches.",
   "visual": "dark",
   "start": 9.202,
   "end": 11.551
  },
  {
   "text": "So its huge eyes catch every bit of light there is.",
   "visual": "eyes",
   "start": 11.551,
   "end": 14.386
  },
  {
   "text": "Just like an owl hunting at night.",
   "visual": "owl",
   "start": 14.386,
   "end": 16.207
  },
  {
   "text": "Faint glimmers in the dark guide it to food.",
   "visual": "glimmer",
   "start": 16.207,
   "end": 18.538
  },
  {
   "text": "Tiny shrimp and jellies.",
   "visual": "food",
   "start": 18.538,
   "end": 20.259
  },
  {
   "text": "Scientists filmed one with a robot submarine, about twelve hundred meters down.",
   "visual": "rov",
   "start": 20.259,
   "end": 25.088
  },
  {
   "text": "Its scientific name even starts with false, because it was first put in the wrong group.",
   "visual": "name2",
   "start": 25.088,
   "end": 30.076
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow BioNiche for more weird animals.",
   "visual": "cta",
   "start": 30.076,
   "end": 33.17
  }
 ],
